FPAC 4.1.5-rc14 — Build, packaging and documentation cleanup
============================================================

This release contains no functional change to the node itself; it fixes
the source-packaging chain and tidies the documentation.

  * Build: "make dist" and "make distcheck" now work.  The build-only
    helper wp/make_tab (which generates crc_tab.h) was linked against
    ../lib/libfpac.a through the directory-wide LDADD.  Because "make
    dist" generates the BUILT_SOURCES before the libraries are built,
    make_tab could not be linked and dist aborted.  make_tab now has an
    empty per-target LDADD (it only uses stdio); the installed programs
    keep linking against libfpac.a and libax25 exactly as before.

  * Packaging: the top-level Makefile.am gained a "distclean-local" rule
    that removes the autom4te.cache directory, which "make distclean"
    used to leave behind.  Source tarballs are now clean without manual
    intervention.

  * Documentation: README typos fixed, the obsolete TODO entry about
    libax25-0.0.9 compatibility removed, and the bug-report pointer
    reworded (open a GitHub issue, it is not a mailing list).  README.svn
    has been rewritten for git and renamed README.git.

-- Bernard Pidoux <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>  Friday, may 29 2026

Assisted by Claude Opus 4.8 (Anthropic) <noreply@anthropic.com>.

FPAC 4.1.5-rc13 — mailbbs segfault fixes
========================================

Three bugs in tools/mailbbs.c have been corrected.  They all caused
segmentation faults on nodes where linfbb or ROSE kernel support is not
active:

  * NULL pointer dereference: rs_get_addr() returns NULL when the ROSE
    kernel module is not loaded (/proc/net/rose absent).  The result was
    passed directly to rose_aton(), which dereferenced it.  A NULL check
    with a diagnostic message is now performed before the call.

  * NULL pointer dereference on local callsign lookup: if option -i is
    not supplied and *_config_get_addr() returns NULL (port not
    configured), ax25_aton_entry()/ax25_aton() was called with NULL.
    Fixed in the AF_ROSE, AF_NETROM and AF_AX25 branches.

  * Off-by-one buffer overflow in readbbs(): when a received line exactly
    fills the buffer, the null terminator was written one byte past the
    end of the caller's stack buffer.  Fixed by using pos (bytes actually
    written) rather than nb (the raw byte count) for the null terminator,
    and by passing sizeof(buf)-1 from main() to reserve one byte of
    headroom.

-- Bernard Pidoux <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>  Tuesday, may 26 2026

FPAC 4.1.5-rc12 — Configurable display colours
===============================================

First of all : you can disable colors in fpacnode with command "col"

fpacnode now reads an optional colour configuration file at startup:

    /usr/local/etc/ax25/fpacnode.colors

This file lets the sysop customise every colour used in the node's
interactive display without recompiling.  If the file is absent, all
colours fall back to the built-in defaults (identical to rc11).

WHAT CAN BE CONFIGURED
-----------------------

  [banniere]   — connection banner: version number, node name, hello/info text
  [tableaux]   — table elements: column headers, callsigns, ROSE/NET-ROM
                 addresses, port names, timestamps
  [ax25]       — AX.25 link states: Disconnected, Conn pending, Disc pending,
                 Connected, Recovery, Unknown
  [rose]       — ROSE circuit state: Connected / idle (-----)
  [netrom]     — NET-ROM neighbour status: Connected / idle (-----)
  [qualite]    — route quality: good (>50%), medium (1-50%), none (0%)
  [indicateurs]— boolean flags: yes / no  (e.g. restart column)

COLOUR NAMES
------------

Foreground (text) colours:
  noir  rouge_fonce  vert_fonce  jaune_fonce  bleu_fonce  magenta_fonce
  cyan_fonce  gris  gris_fonce  rouge  vert  jaune  bleu  magenta  cyan
  blanc  defaut

Background colours (prefix with "fond_"):
  fond_noir  fond_rouge_fonce  fond_vert_fonce  fond_jaune_fonce
  fond_bleu_fonce  fond_magenta_fonce  fond_cyan_fonce  fond_gris
  fond_gris_fonce  fond_rouge  fond_vert  fond_jaune  fond_bleu
  fond_magenta  fond_cyan  fond_blanc  fond_defaut

SYNTAX
------

Each line has the form:

    key = foreground_colour [+ background_colour]   # optional comment

Examples:

    version      = rouge
    connected    = noir + fond_vert
    disconnected = vert + fond_rouge

Unknown colour names are silently ignored; the built-in default is kept.

TOOLS
-----

Two Python utilities are provided in the source tree:

  fpacnode_colors.py
      Displays the full ANSI palette and a live preview of the current
      colour assignments as they would appear in the node.
      Run:  python3 fpacnode_colors.py

  generate_colors_conf.py
      Regenerates /usr/local/etc/ax25/fpacnode.colors.  Each line's
      comment contains the colour name rendered in its own ANSI colour,
      so a plain "cat" of the file is self-documenting.
      Run:  sudo python3 generate_colors_conf.py

      An alternative destination can be given as first argument:
        python3 generate_colors_conf.py -          (stdout preview)
        sudo python3 generate_colors_conf.py /path/to/file

NOTES
-----

* The COlor command (minimum 2 letters) still toggles coloured output
  ON/OFF at runtime; fpacnode.colors only changes which colours are used,
  not whether they are enabled.

* The file is read once at startup, immediately after fpac.conf.
  A restart of fpacnode is required to apply changes.

* Colour sequences in the comment field of fpacnode.colors are embedded
  as real ANSI escape bytes; editors that interpret escape codes (less -R,
  most terminal emulators) will render them.  Plain text editors simply
  show the raw ESC sequences without harm.

-- Bernard Pidoux <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>  Saturday, may 24 2026
